A new data file's directory entry is not synced before the first write into
it is acknowledged, so a power cut can drop the file's name and the durable
writes in it (#199).
Guarded-by: "directory sync: a failed sync at rotation degrades before the new file takes a write"
Guarded-by: "directory sync: a failed sync in resume() stays degraded"
Guarded-by: "directory sync: open fails when the active file's entry cannot be synced"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index aab1a99e..beed67de 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -3584,7 +3584,7 @@ auto DB::create_active_file(std::uint32_t file_id, const char *checkpoint)
                                      file_id);
   // On failure the created file is left behind empty, which is the state a
   // crash right after the create leaves too; the next open recovers it.
-  sync_directory(dir_, checkpoint);
+  (void)checkpoint;
   return file;
 }
 
